  "fixture_id": "cdg-night-layover",
  "title": "Four hours is not four hours: the same layover length at CDG at 01:40, LHR at midday, and AMS at midday",
  "pins_down": "Layover cost is keyed by (airport, arrival hall, departure hall, LOCAL CLOCK TIME, onward Schengen status), never by duration. Three options here carry a layover within 10 minutes of the same length; if the scorer prices them similarly, the layover model is a duration scalar wearing a costume and the product has no moat.",
  "as_of": "2026-03-01",
  "notes": [
    "THE BRIEF'S HEADLINE EXAMPLE CANNOT BE BOOKED. 'Four hours at CDG arriving 1:40am' is not a schedulable itinerary: CDG has a night movement ban under the 2003 arretes - arrivals are prohibited on-block 00:30-05:29 local, departures off-block 00:00-04:59. The latest legal SCHEDULED arrival is 00:29. A 01:40 arrival exists only as a delay. Worse, no NYC-CDG nonstop could produce it anyway - eastbound transatlantic is structurally either a redeye landing 06:00-13:30 or a day flight landing 20:00-22:30, so the 00:30-05:30 window is empty of scheduled passenger arrivals by construction.",
    "So this fixture builds it honestly: a SCHEDULED 00:10 arrival, which is legal with 20 minutes to spare, and an ACTUAL on-block of 01:40 after a 90-minute delay. Ranking runs on the scheduled times; risk_adjustment runs on the delay. One fixture, both, without either lying.",
    "All flight numbers here are synthetic and flagged as such. Borrowing a real number and giving it invented times produces a fixture that looks authoritative and is wrong - which is worse than one that is obviously made up.",
    "The CDG option is also sold with a 65-minute connection at LHR against a published 90-minute T3-to-T5 minimum. Booking sites sell these. That is a separate defect from the layover and gets its own ledger line.",
    "What makes the CDG case punishing is not the hour by itself. It is that a US-to-CDG-to-Schengen passenger clears immigration at CDG, which ejects them from the 2E transit zone at an hour when the 2F security checkpoint is not open and landside Terminal 2 will not re-admit them from outside. Neither properly airside nor able to leave. A 2E-to-2E connection at the same minute stays airside all night and is a completely different object.",
    "MCT figures here are CITED, not verified - the official IATA table was not reachable. Marked so, because a grade that turns on MCT margin should not rest on a number nobody checked."
  ],

